<CapyPlopInfo title="Privacy policy" description="How Capy Plop handles local gameplay saves, purchases, RevenueCat, optional house ads, campaign links and support requests.">
  <p>This policy covers the Capy Plop iOS/iPadOS game and its support pages, provided by Randy Torres under the RandyVentures name. No Capy Plop account is required.</p>
  <h2>Gameplay stays on your device</h2>
  <p>Scores, lifetime plops, perfect streaks, trail stars, challenge medals, outfit choices, settings, hidden-ad preferences and cached promotional content are stored in the app's private local storage. The game does not upload scores or saves to our server and has no cloud-save service or public leaderboard. Your device backups may include app data under your Apple settings.</p>
  <h2>Purchases and RevenueCat</h2>
  <p>Apple processes the optional Hot Springs Pass purchase. The app uses verified StoreKit transactions for purchased access and restoration. We do not receive your payment-card number or Apple Account password.</p>
  <p>RevenueCat receives purchase history and a randomly generated app user identifier for purchase functionality, restoration support, fraud prevention and purchase/revenue reporting. Records can include product and transaction identifiers, purchase dates, currency/storefront, purchase/refund status, and technical information such as app, operating-system and SDK versions. Connection information is processed when communicating with these services. We can view these purchase records and reports in RevenueCat.</p>
  <p>The app does not supply RevenueCat with your name, email, scores, contacts, advertising identifier or a custom account identifier. Its generated purchase identifier is not tied to a Capy Plop login. If you voluntarily send your Purchase support ID to support, we can use it to locate your purchase record and associate that request with the contact information you provide. We do not use purchase records to target promotions or follow you across apps.</p>
  <p>See <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy/">RevenueCat's privacy policy</a> for their practices.</p>
  <h2>Optional promotions for our other apps</h2>
  <p>Capy Plop can show clearly labeled native ads for other apps by Randy Torres. Watching the stated time can earn one continue. Opening a link or downloading an advertised app is optional and is never required for the reward. Fresh attempts are unlimited.</p>
  <p>The app requests a catalog and artwork over HTTPS from randyventures.com, hosted on GitHub Pages. Its host processes ordinary network request information, including IP address, requested path, time and connection/browser information where provided, to deliver and protect the service. The app accepts data and images, not remote JavaScript or executable game code. Cached and bundled content may be used offline.</p>
  <p>Promotion selection uses the available catalog, age-suitability checks, local rotation and ads you have hidden. It does not use your purchase history, location, advertising identifier, contacts or installed-app inventory. The game sends no ad-view, timer-completion, click or gameplay analytics events to our servers. No third-party advertising SDK or cross-app tracking is configured.</p>
  <p>About this ad explains selection and offers local hiding and reporting. If you choose Report, your selected email/share app receives the report you choose to send. A report is not sent automatically. We receive the information and contact details you include when you send it.</p>
  <h2>Optional App Store campaign links</h2>
  <p>If you choose to visit an advertised app, its Apple link includes a shared provider token and a campaign name identifying the app and placement, such as a rewarded promotion or Settings recommendation. Those tags contain no player, device, score, run or purchase-support identifier. Apple can report attributed downloads in aggregate under its own reporting rules. Watching a promotion without opening the link does not attribute a download. We do not receive the identity of people who download an app through a campaign report or join those reports to your RevenueCat purchase record.</p>
  <h2>Support and sharing</h2>
  <p>If you contact us, we receive the email address and information you choose to send, such as a problem description, optional purchase-support identifier, screenshot or ad report. We use it to respond, troubleshoot, handle privacy requests and investigate inappropriate content. Support email is handled through Gmail. Please omit passwords, payment details and other private information unrelated to the request.</p>
  <p>The game can open Apple's share sheet when you choose to share a result. Your chosen destination receives the content you send under its own terms. The app does not upload that share to our server.</p>
  <h2>These web pages</h2>
  <p>These pages are hosted on GitHub Pages, whose infrastructure processes ordinary connection and access information. The site's fonts load from Google Fonts, which receives the requests needed to deliver them. A display-theme preference may be stored in your browser. We have not added advertising trackers or visitor analytics to these Capy Plop pages.</p>
  <p>Provider information: <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub privacy statement</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <h2>Your choices, retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>Use Settings to change sound, haptics and controls, or reset local progress. Reset is destructive and does not cancel or remove a valid purchase. Hiding an ad changes only that device's preferences. Deleting the app removes its local data; copies may remain in backups controlled through your Apple settings. Purchased access and Apple/RevenueCat transaction records are separate from local saves.</p>
  <p>We and our service providers retain support correspondence and purchase records as needed to operate purchase/support functions, meet legal requirements, prevent fraud and resolve disputes. Retention and deletion also depend on Apple, RevenueCat, Gmail and hosting-provider processes. Contact us to request access, correction or deletion of information we or our processors hold. We may need limited information to locate and verify the relevant record and will explain any legal or technical limits. We cannot directly read or recover your local gameplay save.</p>
  <p>We do not sell personal information or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. Service providers may process information in the United States or other countries. No storage or transmission system is completely secure. Depending on where you live, you may have additional privacy rights, including the right to complain to a relevant authority.</p>
  <h2>General audience and changes</h2>
  <p>Capy Plop is a general-audience game and is not directed at children under 13 or offered as a Kids Category implementation. If you believe a child has sent personal information to us, contact us so we can address it. We will update this page when practices change and provide any further notice required by law.</p>
